rdmak, the kernel RDMA verbs framework, follows the Linux kernel verbs
programming model.  The files below are derived from Linux
v6.18-rc2-10-g552c50713f27, commit 552c50713f273b494ac6c77052032a49bc9255e2,
and are used under the OpenIB.org BSD license that each source offers; see
THIRDPARTYLICENSE.  Each source's blob ID at that commit is given.

    rdk.h        include/rdma/ib_verbs.h
                 6139223e92e4c2f26686595279836af20a261da5
                 "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR Linux-OpenIB"
                 The object, attribute, work request and completion shapes
                 and the enum values (the uverbs values come from
                 include/uapi/rdma/ib_user_verbs.h,
                 3b7bd99813e9526ead3f9fb124835a0b17e4d2a6, "(GPL-2.0 WITH
                 Linux-syscall-note) OR Linux-OpenIB").  Names carry the
                 rdk_ prefix; the ops vector and prototypes are illumos.

    rdk_verbs.c  drivers/infiniband/core/verbs.c
                 3a5f81402d2f8b3243fb69a103400bc437bf1354
                 Dual GPL-2.0 / OpenIB.org BSD license text.
                 The QP state table and rdk_modify_qp_is_ok() (from
                 qp_state_table and ib_modify_qp_is_ok(), cut to RC, UD and
                 GSI), rdk_sg_to_pages() (from ib_sg_to_pages(), walking DMA
                 cookies instead of a scatterlist) and the drain functions
                 (from __ib_drain_sq() and __ib_drain_rq()).

    rdk_ibcm_fsm.c, rdk_ibcm_fsm.h
                 drivers/infiniband/core/cm.c
                 01bede8ba105535da9025ba75c392e3e9b161306
                 "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR Linux-OpenIB"
                 The IB CM connection states (enum ib_cm_state) and the
                 answer to each message in each state: cm_req_handler(),
                 cm_dup_req_handler(), cm_rep_handler(),
                 cm_dup_rep_handler(), cm_rtu_handler(), cm_rej_handler(),
                 cm_mra_handler(), cm_dreq_handler(), cm_drep_handler(),
                 cm_destroy_id(), cm_process_send_error(),
                 cm_enter_timewait(), cm_convert_to_ms() and
                 cm_ack_timeout().  The state machine does no I/O.

    rdk_ibcm_msg.c, rdk_ibcm_msg.h
                 include/rdma/ibta_vol1_c12.h
                 960c86bec76c8da7a1db5e8b4a9aa6bf239bdb20
                 "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR Linux-OpenIB"
                 The field offsets and widths of REQ, MRA, REJ, REP, RTU,
                 DREQ and DREP (IBTA vol 1 tables 106 to 113).
                 drivers/infiniband/core/cm_msgs.h
                 8462de7ca26ebadcbdeae43a9b1be517bfb00763
                 "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR Linux-OpenIB"
                 The CM class version, attribute IDs and message codes.
                 drivers/infiniband/core/cma.c
                 5b2d3ae3f9fce85baa71214242658d12f3b87460
                 "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR Linux-OpenIB"
                 struct cma_hdr, CMA_VERSION and the RDMA_PS_TCP service
                 ID; the parser and builder are written for illumos.

    rdk_cm_roce.c, rdk_cm_roce_rx.c, rdk_cm_roce.h
                 drivers/infiniband/core/cm.c
                 01bede8ba105535da9025ba75c392e3e9b161306
                 drivers/infiniband/core/cma.c
                 5b2d3ae3f9fce85baa71214242658d12f3b87460
                 The REQ and REP contents (cm_format_req(), cm_format_rep(),
                 cma_connect_ib(), cma_accept_ib()), the QP attributes of
                 each transition (cm_init_qp_init_attr(),
                 cm_init_qp_rtr_attr(), cm_init_qp_rts_attr()), the
                 duplicate and stale checks (cm_match_req(),
                 cm_insert_remote_id(), cm_insert_remote_qpn()), the
                 stateless replies (cm_issue_rej(), cm_issue_drep()) and the
                 cma.c constants CMA_CM_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT, CMA_MAX_CM_RETRIES
                 and CMA_IBOE_PACKET_LIFETIME.  The tables, locking, timers,
                 QP leases, address binding and passive path resolution are
                 written for illumos.

rdk_device.c, rdk_cq.c, rdk_impl.h, rdk_cm.c, rdk_cm_listen.c, rdk_cm_iw.c,
rdk_cm_addr.c, rdk_cm_gid.c, rdk_cm_gidtab.c, rdk_cm_gidtab.h, rdk_gsi.c,
rdk_gsi.h and rdk_cm_impl.h are written for illumos under the CDDL.  The GID
table from IP events (Linux roce_gid_mgmt.c) and address resolution (Linux
addr.c) are native, as the design requires, and take no code from Linux or
FreeBSD.  rdk_gsi.c is a GSI agent for the CM class only and takes no code
from Linux mad.c.
rdk_cq.c is not derived from Linux drivers/infiniband/core/cq.c, which is
GPL-2.0 only, nor from FreeBSD's ib_cq.c, which was taken from it.

No other Linux or FreeBSD file is used, in particular none of the generic
include/linux headers, rw.c, mr_pool.c or cq.c.
